    "title": "HHS to Send Funds to States Only with Justification, Citing Welfare Fraud Concerns",
    "text": "• Alex Adams, Assistant Secretary for the Administration for Children and Families (ACF), stated that funds will be sent to states only when they can justify the payment.\n• Adams cited the $9 billion welfare fraud scandal in Minnesota as a concern.\n• The Child Care Development Fund, which sends $185 million annually to Minnesota for childcare support, is under investigation.\n• ACF is taking steps to prevent theft of funds sent to states.\n• A tip line has been established at childcare.gov to report fraud, waste, and abuse.\n• Over 75 reports were received within the first few hours of the tip line's launch.\n• ACF activated the \"Defend the Spend\" initiative, requiring photo evidence or receipts for payments.\n• A letter was sent to Minnesota requesting information on daycares suspected of fraud, including licensing inspection reports and internal fraud records.\n• Adams criticized Minnesota Gov. Tim Walz.\n• Previous letters requesting information from the state went unanswered.\n• A temporary freeze on payments was implemented until information justifies the payments.",
